Z||000000||JohnnyK||12-12-2000||12:04 PM||||Well, I've decided I'm going to learn how to skate (sick of making an ass of myself, although it is rather entertaining). Someone give me a quick surefire way to make a good icerink in my backyard... What about those sprinklers that sway back and forth slowly?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jimmy||12-12-2000||03:08 PM||||1.Shovel out an area on the most level part of your yard.  <BR>2.Use the snow to make banks.<BR>3.Get out the hose and start to flood the area.  Try to do it at least twice every morning and twice at night.  Just make sure you cover the entire surface with water.<BR>4.Should have ice to skate on within a couple days.(6-7 floodings of rink)<BR>Make sure you bring the hose inside after flooding as it will freeze and crack outside.  Also if you are using an outside faucet be sure and shut it off from inside the house(shut off valve) otherwise you make crack your pipes if the water freezes.  Also come spring, you WILL have a pond in your yard.  This is OK as long as kids, pets, fieros, ect. stay off of it untill the water seeps away.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Have fun & be CAREFUL who you let skate on it.  Our family used to do this every year untill somebody wanted to sue us for sustaining injuries on our rink.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <BR>Good luck<P>Jim <BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT<BR>||||reg||1
